# Billi platform-level configuration.
#
# GEMINI_API_KEY powers the platform's own AI Intelligence Layer
# (services/context-engine) — this is NOT a per-user or per-operator secret.
# The platform itself runs on Gemini; whoever deploys/submits this build
# supplies one key here and every session, every scenario, and every role
# (protected person, guardian, responder) shares the same live Gemini
# integration through the gateway.
#
# Get a key: https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
# Copy this file to .env (gitignored) and fill in the real value.

GEMINI_API_KEY=

# ADMIN_KEY gates the one route that reads back sensitive aggregate data
# (GET /api/v1/tester-feedback — everyone's submitted feedback/contact info).
# Unset means that route stays closed (503), not silently open. Pick any
# long random string; append it as ?key=<value> when you check submissions.
ADMIN_KEY=

# TWILIO_* powers real SMS delivery for anyone without the native Android
# app installed — most importantly iOS, which can never get that path at
# all (no third-party app may send SMS on iOS without a manual tap, ever).
# Sign up at https://www.twilio.com (free trial credit), grab the Account
# SID + Auth Token from the console, and the phone number Twilio assigns
# you. Unset means this fallback stays off (the native app path, where
# available, is unaffected). Real, ongoing per-message cost once trial
# credit runs out — this is the one place in the platform that costs
# money per use, by design, since there's no free way to reach an
# arbitrary phone number's SMS inbox from a backend.
TWILIO_ACCOUNT_SID=
TWILIO_AUTH_TOKEN=
TWILIO_FROM_NUMBER=
